// Environment: working directories, python, access rules.

%locale: 
%namespace: env

access_denied: Access denied
access_rules.hint: Access rules override default permissions for specific directories. More specific rules (longer paths) take precedence over broader ones. To deny access to a directory, uncheck all permissions (Read, Write, Execute) for that rule.
active: Active
add_access_rule: Add access rule
add_working_directory: Add working directory
additional_settings: Additional settings
bash.environments: Bash
bash.executable_hint: Path to bash.exe (empty = discover)
bash.executable_script: Bash executable
bash.hint: Configure the bash used for running .sh addons. Left empty, discovery prefers Git Bash over the WSL stub and only then falls back to a bash from PATH.
bash.in_use: In use:
bash.select_executable: Select the bash executable
browse: Browse...
check.error: Environment check failed
check.success: Environment is ready
check_configuration: Check configuration
directory_access_rules: Directory Access Rules
enabled: Enabled
execute: Execute
move_down: Move down
move_up: Move up
name: Name
open_in_explorer: Open in explorer
path: Path
powershell.environments: PowerShell
powershell.executable_hint: Path to pwsh or powershell.exe (empty = discover)
powershell.executable_script: PowerShell executable
powershell.hint: Configure the PowerShell used for running .ps1 addons. Left empty, discovery prefers pwsh (PowerShell 7+) on every platform and only then falls back to Windows PowerShell 5.1.
powershell.in_use: In use:
powershell.select_executable: Select the PowerShell executable
python.environments: Python Environments
python.hint: Configure Python virtual environments for script execution. The native venv runs the built-in python tools; an optional second venv isolates Python addons (tools, slash commands and prompt contexts).
python.addon_venv_hint: Path to activate.bat (optional)
python.addon_venv_script: Python addons venv activate script
python.select_addon_venv_script: Select the Python venv activation script for addons
python.select_venv_script: Select Python Venv activation script
python.venv_hint: Path to activate.bat
python.venv_script: Native tools venv activate script
read: Read
remove: Remove
select_script: Select script
select_working_directory: Select working directory
workdir.hint: Working directories define folders the assistant can access. The active directory (selected via radio button) serves as the root for relative paths - all file operations use this directory as the base. You can add multiple directories; the agent can switch between them automatically using its tools.
workdir.title: Working Directories
write: Write
